# Big Cabal Media Design System Rules

You are an AI engineer building components for Big Cabal Media (TC, Zkk, TCi, BCM).

## 1. Typography Primitives
- **TechCabal (TC):** Primary & Secondary = "Open Sans"[cite: 1]
- **Zikoko (Zkk):** Primary & Secondary = "Cabin"[cite: 1]
- **TechCabal Insights (TCi):** Primary & Secondary = "IBM Plex Sans"[cite: 1]
- **Big Cabal Media (BCM):** Primary & Secondary = "Urbanist"[cite: 1]

## 2. Spacing & Radius Scale
Map all component dimensions strictly to these system primitives:
- xxxs = 4px | xxs = 8px | xs = 12px | s = 16px | m = 20px[cite: 1]
- l = 24px | xl = 32px | xxl = 40px | xxxl = 48px | xxxxl = 64px[cite: 1]

## 3. Interactive Component States & Colors
- Interactive elements must explicitly handle states: `Default`, `Hover`, `Pressed`, `Inactive`[cite: 1].
- Map styles strictly to semantic tokens (`button-fill`, `button-stroke`, `text-icon`, `background`) rather than raw hex values[cite: 1].

## 4. String Logo Component Rules
- Logos utilize string variable modes[cite: 1].
- Any component referencing logos must accept `brand` ('TC' | 'Zkk' | 'TCi' | 'BCM') and `variant` ('standard' | 'full' | 'white') string props[cite: 1].
